steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1785150335
      nanos: 815792095
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Section 1: Project Identity & Visual System\n\n* **System Name:** CariCloud (Generic Web-Based Point-of-Sale System for Local Cafeteria / Eatery Operations).\n\n\n* **Target Domain:** Internal operations for Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), specifically localized carinderias and cafeterias in Marikina City.\n\n\n* **Design Paradigm:** High-speed efficiency and micro-entrepreneur accessibility. The UI must be exceptionally clean, modern, and deeply intuitive for users with beginner-to-moderate digital literacy. Focus on highly readable, action-oriented touch targets over dense data charts.\n\n\n* **Color Palette & Material Styling:**\n* **Primary Accent:** Vibrant, clean Orange ranges (`#E65100` to `#FF6D00`) used intentionally for primary calls-to-action, active statuses, and branding emblems.\n* **Secondary Tone:** Warm Amber/Terracotta (`#F57C00`) for navigation elements and secondary interactive toggles.\n* **Surface Neutrals:** Clean, modern Off-Whites and soft Cream surfaces to serve as backgrounds, minimizing eye strain during fast-paced peak hours.\n* **Typography:** Large, highly legible sans-serif typefaces with clear contrast ratios to optimize readability in dynamic kitchen and counter environments.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Section 2: Core Architecture & Configuration\n\n### 2.1 Three-Tier Web Setup\n\nGenerate a fully responsive, cross-platform web application framework optimized for modern mobile and desktop web browsers (Android, iOS, PC). The software architecture must support a frontend presentation layer connected via asynchronous API calls to a robust backend logic engine (ASP.NET Core Web API) with a persistent relational database infrastructure (MySQL). Implement IndexedDB for local storage to save data during internet outages and sync once the connection is restored.\n\n### 2.2 Account Configuration & Multi-Tenancy\n\nThe system serves exclusively as an internal operational tool, entirely removing any public-facing marketplace features. The initial onboarding flow must require the Administrator (Owner) to configure the operational path:\n\n1. **Single Operator Mode:** Synthesizes the Admin and Staff workflows into a single unified workspace, allowing solo owners to run sales and backend management concurrently without switching accounts.\n\n\n2. **Multi-Tenant Mode:** Activates multi-user profile generation, allowing the owner to add distinct employee accounts into their specific POS instance. This strictly separates the Administrator\'s absolute governance over system parameters from the Operational Staff\'s (Cashier) transaction-focused workspace.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Section 3: Detailed Module Specifications\n\n### 3.1 Menu Management & Synchronization\n\n* **Internal Menu Digitization:** Provide an administrative grid interface to transfer rotating daily menus into the system, categorized by dish type (e.g., Ulam, Rice, Drinks).\n\n\n* **Dynamic Modifiers & Portion Scaling:** Allow system operators to define and link specific menu item variations (e.g., extra rice, egg toppings) directly within the cashier workspace. Implement a responsive line-item toggle switch that programmatically divides or adjusts a product\'s base price when marked as a half-order portion.\n\n\n* **Real-time Stock Indicators:** Enable the Admin to manually toggle \"Sold Out\" badges on menu items to immediately prevent the ordering of depleted dishes in the cashier interface.\n\n\n\n### 3.2 High-Speed Order & Transaction Module\n\n* **Peak-Hour Interface:** Build a high-speed \"Quick-Keys\" or high-visibility button interface optimized for a strict three-tap transaction process to ensure the fastest possible checkout during lunch rushes.\n\n\n* **Statutory Discount Processing:** Integrate a one-click digital calculation toggle for national Senior Citizen and PWD discounts that automatically applies a 20% reduction and removes the 12% VAT.\n\n\n* **Multi-Modal Payment Gateway:** Isolate order processing at the transaction level with three clear settlement paths:\n\n\n* *Cash:* Standard rapid-log transaction.\n* *E-Wallet (Paymongo API):* Dynamically generates standard QR Ph codes on checkout, automatically executing asynchronous payment verification via webhook before an order is programmatically marked as paid.\n\n\n* *Credit (Listahan):* Requires a strict Credit Permission Gateway; if the customer is not approved or exceeds their limit, prompt a mandatory Admin/Manager digital override before the transaction can finalize.\n\n\n\n\n\n### 3.3 Analytics, Compliance & Debt Monitoring Module\n\n* **End-of-Day Financial Reconciliation:** Construct a dedicated close-of-day auditing interface. The system must prompt the owner to input absolute daily cash earnings and explicitly log the remaining quantities of unsold dishes (food wastage). The backend must then compute exact net profit margins less the calibrated product loss value.\n\n\n* **Real-Time Debt/Credit Ledger:** A digital tracking dashboard for unsettled customer payments, displaying an authorized credit log to completely replace paper notebooks.\n\n\n* **Local Tax Relief Eligibility Tracker:** Develop a localized compliance tracker that maintains a running total of annual gross sales. It must trigger an alert if the business approaches the \342\202\261250,000 threshold defined by Marikina\'s 2026 tax relief policy.\n\n\n* **Automated BPLO Reporting:** Aggregate historical logs to automatically output downloadable gross sales tax declarations matching the exact documentation layouts required by the Marikina Business Permits and Licensing Office (BPLO).\n\n\n\n### 3.4 Sustainable Tiered Subscription Framework\n\nIntegrate a Three-Tiered SaaS (Software as a Service) monetization model with corresponding feature locks:\n\n* **Tier 1 (\342\202\26149):** Unlocks core operational tools, including the high-speed transaction model, standard end-of-day reports, and statutory Senior/PWD discount processing.\n\n\n* **Tier 2 (\342\202\26199):** Unlocks internal UI personalization, allowing Administrators to modify the POS color scheme (Dark/Light/Store-Specific) and customize the dashboard.\n\n\n* **Tier 3 (\342\202\261199):** Unlocks the Marikina Tax Relief Tracker for strict legal compliance monitoring and automated BPLO sales form generation.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Section 4: Operational Boundaries & Technical Constraints\n\n> ### \342\232\240\357\270\217 Critical System Limitations (Enforce Strictly)\n> \n> \n> 1. **Internal Use Only:** The system is strictly an internal tool for on-site operations; do not generate any customer-facing portals, marketplaces, or online ordering environments.\n> \n> \n> 2. **No Automated Forecasting:** The system relies entirely on rule-based logic for calculations. Do not integrate Artificial Intelligence for predictive modeling or future sales forecasting.\n> \n> \n> 3. **Restricted Inventory Scope:** Do not build ingredient-level inventory tracking (e.g., raw material weights or sub-component tracking). Inventory monitoring is strictly limited to manual \"Sold Out\" badges and the End-of-Day logging of unsold completed dishes.\n> \n> \n> 4. **No HR/Payroll Functionality:** The system must not calculate employee salaries, wages, or track clock-in/out times.\n> \n> \n> \n>"
    items {
      text: "Section 1: Project Identity & Visual System\n\n* **System Name:** CariCloud (Generic Web-Based Point-of-Sale System for Local Cafeteria / Eatery Operations).\n\n\n* **Target Domain:** Internal operations for Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), specifically localized carinderias and cafeterias in Marikina City.\n\n\n* **Design Paradigm:** High-speed efficiency and micro-entrepreneur accessibility. The UI must be exceptionally clean, modern, and deeply intuitive for users with beginner-to-moderate digital literacy. Focus on highly readable, action-oriented touch targets over dense data charts.\n\n\n* **Color Palette & Material Styling:**\n* **Primary Accent:** Vibrant, clean Orange ranges (`#E65100` to `#FF6D00`) used intentionally for primary calls-to-action, active statuses, and branding emblems.\n* **Secondary Tone:** Warm Amber/Terracotta (`#F57C00`) for navigation elements and secondary interactive toggles.\n* **Surface Neutrals:** Clean, modern Off-Whites and soft Cream surfaces to serve as backgrounds, minimizing eye strain during fast-paced peak hours.\n* **Typography:** Large, highly legible sans-serif typefaces with clear contrast ratios to optimize readability in dynamic kitchen and counter environments.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Section 2: Core Architecture & Configuration\n\n### 2.1 Three-Tier Web Setup\n\nGenerate a fully responsive, cross-platform web application framework optimized for modern mobile and desktop web browsers (Android, iOS, PC). The software architecture must support a frontend presentation layer connected via asynchronous API calls to a robust backend logic engine (ASP.NET Core Web API) with a persistent relational database infrastructure (MySQL). Implement IndexedDB for local storage to save data during internet outages and sync once the connection is restored.\n\n### 2.2 Account Configuration & Multi-Tenancy\n\nThe system serves exclusively as an internal operational tool, entirely removing any public-facing marketplace features. The initial onboarding flow must require the Administrator (Owner) to configure the operational path:\n\n1. **Single Operator Mode:** Synthesizes the Admin and Staff workflows into a single unified workspace, allowing solo owners to run sales and backend management concurrently without switching accounts.\n\n\n2. **Multi-Tenant Mode:** Activates multi-user profile generation, allowing the owner to add distinct employee accounts into their specific POS instance. This strictly separates the Administrator\'s absolute governance over system parameters from the Operational Staff\'s (Cashier) transaction-focused workspace.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Section 3: Detailed Module Specifications\n\n### 3.1 Menu Management & Synchronization\n\n* **Internal Menu Digitization:** Provide an administrative grid interface to transfer rotating daily menus into the system, categorized by dish type (e.g., Ulam, Rice, Drinks).\n\n\n* **Dynamic Modifiers & Portion Scaling:** Allow system operators to define and link specific menu item variations (e.g., extra rice, egg toppings) directly within the cashier workspace. Implement a responsive line-item toggle switch that programmatically divides or adjusts a product\'s base price when marked as a half-order portion.\n\n\n* **Real-time Stock Indicators:** Enable the Admin to manually toggle \"Sold Out\" badges on menu items to immediately prevent the ordering of depleted dishes in the cashier interface.\n\n\n\n### 3.2 High-Speed Order & Transaction Module\n\n* **Peak-Hour Interface:** Build a high-speed \"Quick-Keys\" or high-visibility button interface optimized for a strict three-tap transaction process to ensure the fastest possible checkout during lunch rushes.\n\n\n* **Statutory Discount Processing:** Integrate a one-click digital calculation toggle for national Senior Citizen and PWD discounts that automatically applies a 20% reduction and removes the 12% VAT.\n\n\n* **Multi-Modal Payment Gateway:** Isolate order processing at the transaction level with three clear settlement paths:\n\n\n* *Cash:* Standard rapid-log transaction.\n* *E-Wallet (Paymongo API):* Dynamically generates standard QR Ph codes on checkout, automatically executing asynchronous payment verification via webhook before an order is programmatically marked as paid.\n\n\n* *Credit (Listahan):* Requires a strict Credit Permission Gateway; if the customer is not approved or exceeds their limit, prompt a mandatory Admin/Manager digital override before the transaction can finalize.\n\n\n\n\n\n### 3.3 Analytics, Compliance & Debt Monitoring Module\n\n* **End-of-Day Financial Reconciliation:** Construct a dedicated close-of-day auditing interface. The system must prompt the owner to input absolute daily cash earnings and explicitly log the remaining quantities of unsold dishes (food wastage). The backend must then compute exact net profit margins less the calibrated product loss value.\n\n\n* **Real-Time Debt/Credit Ledger:** A digital tracking dashboard for unsettled customer payments, displaying an authorized credit log to completely replace paper notebooks.\n\n\n* **Local Tax Relief Eligibility Tracker:** Develop a localized compliance tracker that maintains a running total of annual gross sales. It must trigger an alert if the business approaches the \342\202\261250,000 threshold defined by Marikina\'s 2026 tax relief policy.\n\n\n* **Automated BPLO Reporting:** Aggregate historical logs to automatically output downloadable gross sales tax declarations matching the exact documentation layouts required by the Marikina Business Permits and Licensing Office (BPLO).\n\n\n\n### 3.4 Sustainable Tiered Subscription Framework\n\nIntegrate a Three-Tiered SaaS (Software as a Service) monetization model with corresponding feature locks:\n\n* **Tier 1 (\342\202\26149):** Unlocks core operational tools, including the high-speed transaction model, standard end-of-day reports, and statutory Senior/PWD discount processing.\n\n\n* **Tier 2 (\342\202\26199):** Unlocks internal UI personalization, allowing Administrators to modify the POS color scheme (Dark/Light/Store-Specific) and customize the dashboard.\n\n\n* **Tier 3 (\342\202\261199):** Unlocks the Marikina Tax Relief Tracker for strict legal compliance monitoring and automated BPLO sales form generation.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Section 4: Operational Boundaries & Technical Constraints\n\n> ### \342\232\240\357\270\217 Critical System Limitations (Enforce Strictly)\n> \n> \n> 1. **Internal Use Only:** The system is strictly an internal tool for on-site operations; do not generate any customer-facing portals, marketplaces, or online ordering environments.\n> \n> \n> 2. **No Automated Forecasting:** The system relies entirely on rule-based logic for calculations. Do not integrate Artificial Intelligence for predictive modeling or future sales forecasting.\n> \n> \n> 3. **Restricted Inventory Scope:** Do not build ingredient-level inventory tracking (e.g., raw material weights or sub-component tracking). Inventory monitoring is strictly limited to manual \"Sold Out\" badges and the End-of-Day logging of unsold completed dishes.\n> \n> \n> 4. **No HR/Payroll Functionality:** The system must not calculate employee salaries, wages, or track clock-in/out times.\n> \n> \n> \n>"
