  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Backend Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the backend architecture for CariCloud. I\'m exploring an Express-based setup, considering whether to use a full `server.ts` file or a more streamlined express router. I\'m also thinking about running Express alongside Vite middleware. I\'m leaning toward a lightweight approach.\n\n\n**Constructing Backend Functionality**\n\nI\'ve decided to create a full-stack backend in `server.ts`. This involves designing the `/api/*` routes. I\'m focusing on features for menu management, transaction processing, statutory discount calculations, and a customer credit ledger. I\'ll also integrate EOD reconciliation, local tax relief tracking, subscription tier management, and the distinction between single operator and multi-tenant mode.\n\n\n**Evaluating Package Updates**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the `package.json` scripts and considering updates for a full-stack custom server setup, particularly `dev`, `build`, and `start`. I\'m also reviewing potential package dependencies, specifically for IndexedDB integration and client-side storage, weighing the benefits of packages like `dexie` or `idb` against a simpler, zero-dependency approach using native IndexedDB or a custom wrapper. My current package list includes `lucide-react`, `motion`, `express`, `dotenv`, `tsx`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, and `@types/node`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 726561273
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
