  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing CariCloud UI**\n\nI\'m starting the build of the modular React UI components for CariCloud! I\'ve begun designing the component files, specifically `/src/components/Header.tsx`. This file will handle the top navigation bar, incorporating the CariCloud logo, a mode toggle between Single Operator and Multi-Tenant, a user switcher (Admin vs. Cashier), and an online/offline sync status badge with a sync trigger.\n\n\n**Expanding POS Module Design**\n\nI\'ve been iterating on the POS Module\'s design. I\'m adding features to `/src/components/POSModule.tsx`, specifically button controls for the Subscription Plan Tier badge and Theme color indicator. I\'m also adding logic for a left-side Category tabs pane, a search bar and Quick-Keys dish grid. The Active Cart order list and the Statutory Discount Section are still in the works. The Pay Now action will trigger a modal!\n\n\n**Refining Payment Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating PayMongo, with GCash/Maya badges and dynamic payment status checks. Ideally, a one-click \"Simulate Webhook Payment\" would be nice for testing! I\'m also including a credit settlement flow with customer selection, credit limit display, and an Admin PIN override if the transaction exceeds the limit, which leads to a receipt modal. I\'m focusing on `/src/components/ReceiptModal.tsx` for a printable preview now.\n\n\n**Developing EOD Reporting**\n\nI\'m now incorporating End-of-Day (EOD) auditing. I\'m focusing on calculating metrics like Expected Gross Sales, Cash Variance, and Total E-Wallet. I will also incorporate a history table for past daily EOD audits.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Building Debt/Credit Ledger**\n\nI\'m developing a digital ledger at `/src/components/ListahanModule.tsx` for tracking customer debt/credit. I\'m building a customer directory with search and filter capabilities, including a record payment modal. I\'m also adding functionality to edit credit limits and add new customers.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Integrating BPLO Tax Module**\n\nI\'m now building the BPLO Tax Module at `/src/components/BploTaxModule.tsx` for Marikina 2026. This module will track progress toward the \342\202\261250,000 threshold and calculate annual and quarterly tax metrics. There will also be an option to download a printable Marikina BPLO Gross Sales Declaration.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 962168687
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
