  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Login Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the login landing page component. Specifically, I\'m fleshing out the design and functionality of `LoginLandingPage.tsx`. It will serve as the gateway, allowing users to select their role and initiate their login flow. I\'ve begun to define the two main login paths. One is for the owner and the other is for the user. I\'ve also thought about how it will allow for Owner PIN Entry.\n\n\n**Defining Login Functionality**\n\nI\'ve moved on from the landing page. Now I am digging into how the login functionality works, specifically for the different user types. I\'m building out a PIN pad with default hints. I\'m also ensuring the design is clean and minimal, using orange, light background, dark text, and light borders, so the application keeps the simple design the users are looking for. I also plan to add the ability to switch accounts or logout from the header at any time. I am focusing on making the process as streamlined as possible.\n\n\n**Analyzing Transactional Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the transactional data display. I\'m focusing on providing users with a clear overview of past transactions. I\'m thinking about including a search input for receipt numbers, customer names, cashiers, and item names. I\'m considering filter options based on payment methods. Additionally, I plan on implementing a table or card view for easy browsing. I\'m also thinking of a quick action button for each receipt to allow viewing or printing. I\'ll need to clearly indicate that these are archived receipts.\n\n\n**Refining Receipt Actions**\n\nI\'m now refining the actions in `ReceiptModal.tsx` upon transaction completion. I\'ve added \"Start New Order (Skip Printing)\" and \"Print Receipt & Start New Order\" buttons. I\'ve also incorporated a note about receipt archival. In `Header.tsx`, I am working on adding a \"Receipts Archive\" tab, making it accessible to both Owners and Employees. I\'m focusing on ensuring navigation tab visibility respects user roles.\n\n\n"
