  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Account-Based Access**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the account-based landing page requirement. This means users, both owners and employees, must log in. This approach aims to prevent security breaches and control access effectively. Right now, I\'m calling it `LoginLandingPage`.\n\n\n**Implementing Account-Based Accounts**\n\nI\'m now implementing the account-based structure. I\'ve defined owner and employee accounts. Owner accounts are now clearly listed. If multi-tenant mode is enabled, employee accounts also appear. Each account card shows the name, avatar/badge, role, and a PIN prompt for sign-in. I\'ll store employee accounts in `LocalStorageDatabase` or `StoreSettings` and defined `registeredEmployees` in `db.ts`. I am considering `UserProfile` structure for each employee.\n\n\n**Defining Default Accounts**\n\nI\'m now defining the default accounts. There\'s a default owner with ID `u-owner`, name \"Ate Maria (Store Owner),\" role `ADMIN`, and PIN `1234`. I\'m also adding a default employee account with ID `u-emp1`, name \"Juana Dela Cruz (Shift Cashier),\" role `CASHIER`, and PIN `0000`. These accounts will be displayed on the login landing page, allowing users to select and sign in securely, including filtering options for owner or employee accounts.\n\n\n"
