    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Request**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s explicit request for the landing page\'s design. The key seems to revolve around an account-based login, involving username/email and password fields. I\'ve noted the \'Forgot Password?\' functionality as well, which will require a password reset mechanism with code confirmation.\n\n\n**Implementing User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user authentication and access control. I\'m adding `email` and `password` fields to the `UserProfile` type in `src/types.ts`. I am also updating the initial staff accounts in `src/data/initialData.ts` to include usernames, emails, and passwords for Owner and Cashier roles. This will be the foundational element for secure login.\n\n\n**Designing the Login Form**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing `LoginLandingPage.tsx`. I\'ve added a robust account-based login form with username/email and password fields. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness by including \'Fill Demo Account\' buttons for easy testing. The login button logic will be case-insensitive, matching user input against the staff accounts array in `src/data/initialData.ts`.\n\n\n**Developing Password Reset**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Forgot Password?\" flow. I\'m adding an error message if the account doesn\'t exist or if the password verification fails. Furthermore, I\'ll provide a clear indication of whether the logged-in user is an owner or cashier. I\'m also designing the three-step reset modal, starting with the email input and verification. I\'ll need to generate and display a simulated email code for testing.\n\n\n**Restricting Access to Listahan**\n\nI am now restricting Listahan access to the owner role. In `Header.tsx`, I\'ll either hide or lock the \"Listahan (Utang)\" navigation item for staff, with a lock icon, or \"Owner Only\" badge and disabling functionality or showing an alert/modal. If a staff member tries to navigate to it, `App.tsx` will display an \"Access Restricted\" banner or redirect. Finally, in `ListahanModule.tsx`, I\'ll check `currentUserRole` to show an access-denied overlay to non-owners.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 357275661
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
