  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Okay, some changes. First, before the login page, there should be a landing page where we click between \"Login as Owner\" and \"Login as Employee\". After clicking, this redirects them to a login page that only accepts either owner or employee accounts respectively. If a user inputs an owner account in the employee login page, it will display \"This is an Owner\'s Account. Please input an Employee Account.\" and vice versa.\n\nSecond, please remove anything related to the PINs in the Settings or the system.\n\nThird, the Listahan tab should be able to be seen by both Owner and Employee, but only editable by the Owner.\n\nFourth, the Staff, Employee, Cashier, or any form of Employee, except the Owner, is the exact same thing."
    items {
      text: "Okay, some changes. First, before the login page, there should be a landing page where we click between \"Login as Owner\" and \"Login as Employee\". After clicking, this redirects them to a login page that only accepts either owner or employee accounts respectively. If a user inputs an owner account in the employee login page, it will display \"This is an Owner\'s Account. Please input an Employee Account.\" and vice versa.\n\nSecond, please remove anything related to the PINs in the Settings or the system.\n\nThird, the Listahan tab should be able to be seen by both Owner and Employee, but only editable by the Owner.\n\nFourth, the Staff, Employee, Cashier, or any form of Employee, except the Owner, is the exact same thing."
    }
  }
}
