  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Login Flow**\n\nI\'ve been sketching out the new login flow for CariCloud. The initial focus is on a clear landing page before login. My plan is to have two distinct options: \"Login as Owner\" and \"Login as Employee\". Each will then lead to a role-specific login form to streamline the process. Role validation will be key to security.\n\n\n**Refining Role-Based Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific error messaging for login attempts. If the user\'s role doesn\'t match the selected login form, I\'ll present a clear, actionable message. For example, *\"This is an Owner\'s Account. Please input an Employee Account.\"* or vice versa, to guide users toward the correct login path. The standard username/password and reset flow remains.\n\n**Eliminating PINs**\n\nThe PIN system is going away entirely. I\'m scrubbing the codebase to remove all PIN-related elements, including settings, database fields, form inputs, and UI references such as `adminPin` and `cashierPin`. Passwords are now the sole authentication method.\n\n**Controlling Listahan Access**\n\nI\'ve clarified the Listahan (Utang) tab access. Both Owners and Employees will see customer ledgers, but only Owners can modify them: adding customers, recording payments, and adjusting credit limits. Employees get a read-only view with disabled actions and clear badges.\n\n\n**Standardizing Terminology Updates**\n\nI\'m now focused on standardizing the terminology for user roles. \"Owner\" will consistently map to `ADMIN`, and \"Employee\" will be `CASHIER` throughout the application. I\'m carefully reviewing the codebase, starting with `/src/types.ts` to ensure consistency in types and attributes. I\'ll need to remove any redundant references to PINs. Next, I\'ll update `/src/components/LoginLandingPage.tsx` to handle the new login cards and error messaging, as well as the forgot password flow. Finally, the Listahan module will be updated.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 951749819
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
