  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requests**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s four requests. The initial focus is on the landing page, specifically the \"portal selection\" aspect. I\'m building out a card-based approach, and am currently developing the initial card/option for \"Login as Owner.\" This includes refining the icon and labeling for clarity and user understanding, to ensure seamless navigation.\n\n\n**Refining Role-Based Login**\n\nI\'m now focusing on role-specific login. The \"Login as Employee\" card is ready, with icon and labeling finalized. Transitioning after login selection, I\'m incorporating a role-specific top pill, e.g., \"OWNER LOGIN\". Crucially, I\'m building out validation logic to prevent role mismatches during login attempts. I\'m verifying the account type against the chosen portal to display appropriate error messages, like \"This is an Owner\'s Account.\"\n\n\n**Implementing Login Validation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the validation process after the user selects a role. I\'m focusing on scenarios where the account type doesn\'t match the selected portal, generating an error message: \"This is an Employee\'s Account. Please input an Owner Account.\" If the role matches, I\'m verifying the password, and constructing messages for success or failure, respectively. Finally, I\'m constructing a \"account not found\" scenario.\n\n**Removing PINs from Settings**\n\nI\'m transitioning to the PIN removal from the system. I\'m starting in `types.ts`, removing `adminPin` and `cashierPin` from `StoreSettings`, and making the `pin` field in `UserProfile` optional or removing it entirely. In `SettingsModule.tsx`, I\'ll remove the \"Security PIN Governance\" section. I\'m also planning to eliminate the PIN fields from the Employee Staff modal, and replacing them with Username, Email, Password, and Role fields. I\'m working now to remove `PinOverrideModal.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 404721493
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
