  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Login Flow**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the initial user prompt, focusing intently on the preliminary login process. I\'m visualizing the desired flow: a distinct landing page precedes the login page, offering clearly labeled options for owner and employee access, with redirection after selection. I\'m verifying all elements of this step are in place.\n\n\n**Designing the Login Page**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the UI design for the login landing page, specifically the `LoginLandingPage.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on a clean and intuitive user experience. I\'m implementing a state variable, `selectedPortal`, that dictates the rendering of either the portal selection screen or the actual login form. Two distinct cards, one for \"Owner\" and one for \"Employee,\" will be the initial prompt. Selection triggers the appropriate login form, and a back button is included.\n\n\n**Validating Login Inputs**\n\nI\'m now deep in the validation logic of the login process, specifically focusing on the input fields and error handling. I\'ve built validation steps for username/email and password, integrating role checks to avoid incorrect account types. Error messages are crafted for both no account and incorrect role scenarios. I\'m ensuring the \'Forgot Password?\' flow is also fully integrated.\n\n\n**Implementing Auto-Fill for Testing**\n\nI\'m working on auto-fill functionality to streamline testing. I\'m focusing on quick auto-fill buttons or pre-labeled fields tailored for the selected portal. This will accelerate the testing process and improve efficiency. This new implementation will assist the other developers in debugging!\n\n\n**Clarifying Access Control**\n\nI\'m now clarifying access control logic, particularly regarding the \"Listahan\" tab. There was a discrepancy in the prompt requirements, but it\'s now clarified. The latest prompt indicates employees can *view* the Listahan, but only the owner can *edit* it. I\'m focusing on implementing role-based restrictions for adding new customers, recording payments, and editing customer details. I\'m implementing role checks in the front-end components, and verifying they align with the backend permissions.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 26369685
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
