    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "System Role: You are an elite UI/UX Architect and Expert Frontend Developer.\nYour Task: You are going to redesign the user interface and frontend component structure of an existing system specification. You must apply the exact design system, aesthetic \"aura,\" and visual language of the target website provided below, while STRICTLY preserving 100% of the original system\'s functionality, features, and constraints.\nTarget Aesthetic Website: https://www.airmee.com/en/?ref=land-book.com\n\360\237\216\250 Part 1: Design & Aura Directives (The \"Airmee\" Skin)\nAnalyze the target website and extract its core UI/UX principles to apply to the system:\nScandinavian Minimalism: Emulate the target site\'s ultra-clean, tech-forward aesthetic. Utilize vast amounts of negative (white) space to let elements breathe. Remove all unnecessary borders, dividing lines, and visual clutter.\nTypographic Hierarchy: Apply a premium, geometric sans-serif font stack. Use oversized, bold, high-contrast headers to guide the user\'s eye, paired with highly legible, slightly muted body text.\nColor Palette Mapping: The system\'s primary brand color relies on clean, modern ranges of orange. You must apply this orange palette using the target site\'s logic: use crisp off-whites (#FAFAFA, #FFFFFF) for primary surfaces, deep slate/blacks for text to create stark contrast, and use the vibrant orange strictly for primary calls-to-action (CTAs), active states, and critical notification badges (like \"Sold Out\" or \"Pending Credit\").\nComponent Styling: Emulate the target site\'s structural elements. Use smoothly rounded corners for containers, soft and diffused drop shadows for floating cards, and pill-shaped touch targets.\nFluidity & Feel: The interface must feel incredibly premium, utilizing smooth, rapid micro-interactions and hover states that feel lightweight and professional.\n\342\232\231\357\270\217 Part 2: Functional Guardrails (The \"Iron Boundary\")\nYou are forbidden from altering the business logic, user pathways, or technical constraints of the provided system. You are applying a visual \"skin\" only.\nDo NOT change, remove, or add to the following:\nScope & Limitations: Do not add external delivery tracking, public marketplace apps, online customer ordering portals, or artificial intelligence algorithms. The system remains strictly an internal tool.\nUser Roles: Maintain the exact configurations for the \"Single Operator\" and \"Multi-Tenant\" (Administrator vs. Operational Staff) roles.\nHardware & Backend: Maintain the exact tech stack: HTML/CSS/Bootstrap frontend, ASP.NET Core backend, MySQL database, and IndexedDB local storage.\nLegal & Tax Logic: The system must retain the exact logic for calculating 20% Senior Citizen/PWD discounts and tracking the Marikina City \342\202\261250,000 annual sales tax relief limit.\nSubscription Model: Maintain the exact Three-Tiered SaaS structure (\342\202\26149, \342\202\26199, \342\202\261199) and their respective feature locks.\n\360\237\223\245 Part 3: The System Payload\nThe last prompt prior to this one is the comprehensive architectural blueprint of the system you are styling. Analyze it carefully, wrap it entirely in the Airmee-inspired visual design system outlined in Part 1, and output a detailed frontend architectural guide and UI component breakdown."
    items {
      text: "System Role: You are an elite UI/UX Architect and Expert Frontend Developer.\nYour Task: You are going to redesign the user interface and frontend component structure of an existing system specification. You must apply the exact design system, aesthetic \"aura,\" and visual language of the target website provided below, while STRICTLY preserving 100% of the original system\'s functionality, features, and constraints.\nTarget Aesthetic Website: https://www.airmee.com/en/?ref=land-book.com\n\360\237\216\250 Part 1: Design & Aura Directives (The \"Airmee\" Skin)\nAnalyze the target website and extract its core UI/UX principles to apply to the system:\nScandinavian Minimalism: Emulate the target site\'s ultra-clean, tech-forward aesthetic. Utilize vast amounts of negative (white) space to let elements breathe. Remove all unnecessary borders, dividing lines, and visual clutter.\nTypographic Hierarchy: Apply a premium, geometric sans-serif font stack. Use oversized, bold, high-contrast headers to guide the user\'s eye, paired with highly legible, slightly muted body text.\nColor Palette Mapping: The system\'s primary brand color relies on clean, modern ranges of orange. You must apply this orange palette using the target site\'s logic: use crisp off-whites (#FAFAFA, #FFFFFF) for primary surfaces, deep slate/blacks for text to create stark contrast, and use the vibrant orange strictly for primary calls-to-action (CTAs), active states, and critical notification badges (like \"Sold Out\" or \"Pending Credit\").\nComponent Styling: Emulate the target site\'s structural elements. Use smoothly rounded corners for containers, soft and diffused drop shadows for floating cards, and pill-shaped touch targets.\nFluidity & Feel: The interface must feel incredibly premium, utilizing smooth, rapid micro-interactions and hover states that feel lightweight and professional.\n\342\232\231\357\270\217 Part 2: Functional Guardrails (The \"Iron Boundary\")\nYou are forbidden from altering the business logic, user pathways, or technical constraints of the provided system. You are applying a visual \"skin\" only.\nDo NOT change, remove, or add to the following:\nScope & Limitations: Do not add external delivery tracking, public marketplace apps, online customer ordering portals, or artificial intelligence algorithms. The system remains strictly an internal tool.\nUser Roles: Maintain the exact configurations for the \"Single Operator\" and \"Multi-Tenant\" (Administrator vs. Operational Staff) roles.\nHardware & Backend: Maintain the exact tech stack: HTML/CSS/Bootstrap frontend, ASP.NET Core backend, MySQL database, and IndexedDB local storage.\nLegal & Tax Logic: The system must retain the exact logic for calculating 20% Senior Citizen/PWD discounts and tracking the Marikina City \342\202\261250,000 annual sales tax relief limit.\nSubscription Model: Maintain the exact Three-Tiered SaaS structure (\342\202\26149, \342\202\26199, \342\202\261199) and their respective feature locks.\n\360\237\223\245 Part 3: The System Payload\nThe last prompt prior to this one is the comprehensive architectural blueprint of the system you are styling. Analyze it carefully, wrap it entirely in the Airmee-inspired visual design system outlined in Part 1, and output a detailed frontend architectural guide and UI component breakdown."
