    thinking: "**Reviewing Successful Build**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the compilation and linting processes for the applet were successful! I\'ve just implemented the dish photo upload fix, enhancing the `handleFileUpload` function within `MenuManagementModule.tsx`. It now automatically scales down large images uploaded, using an offscreen HTML5 canvas element, to a maximum dimension of 600px, which should resolve the upload issues.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have resolved both reported issues in CariCloud POS:\n\n1. **Fixed Dish Photo Upload in Menu Management**:\n   - **Automatic Canvas Compression**: Upgraded `handleFileUpload` in `MenuManagementModule` to automatically resize and compress uploaded image files to a web-optimized 600px JPEG format using HTML5 Canvas. This eliminates local storage quota errors and allows uploading any custom dish image seamlessly.\n   - **Image Controls**: Added instant image preview, a **Remove Photo** button to reset or replace dish images easily, and maintained URL input and preset image pickers.\n\n2. **Added \"Create an Account\" to Owner and Employee Login Pages**:\n   - **Login Entry Points**: Placed a prominent **\"Create an Account\"** button on both the **Owner Login** and **Employee Login** pages, as well as a quick registration option on the main portal selection screen.\n   - **Account Registration Modal**: Implemented an interactive registration modal supporting both **Store Owner (Admin)** and **Employee (Cashier)** account creation with fields for Full Name, Email, Username, Password, Confirm Password, and a 4-Digit Counter Security PIN.\n   - **Validation & Persistence**: Integrated full validation (duplicate account checks, password matching) that saves new accounts to local persistence, pre-fills the login form upon creation, and allows immediate sign-in."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 480787747
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
